<title>SWEDEN: IBM says sells stake in Swedish IBS.</title>
<headline>IBM says sells stake in Swedish IBS.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBM Svenska AB, a Swedish unit of International Business Machines Corp, said on Thursday it sold its 5.3 percent stake of capital in Swedish computer company International Business Systems (IBS).</p>
<p>IBM sold 616,455 series B shares in IBS and 616,455 subscription rights for 123,297 series B shares, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;After this transaction IBM owns neither shares nor subscription rights for shares in IBS,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
